Screening Rules Carried Forward
Four decisions made while building the codebook against the Georgia Tech corpus carry into this synthesis unchanged:
• Instructor-AI arrangements (R2). Instructor uses of AI, such as course preparation or grading, are coded with the same codebook but analyzed separately from learner episodes.
• AI removal (R7). Designs whose only move is to remove AI are excluded. Under a mixed-article provision, documents that remove AI in one place but describe AI-mediated activity elsewhere are retained, and only the AI-mediated parts are coded.
• Non-interactional commentary (R14). Documents in which AI is subject matter, or which describe policy and resource work without any human-AI arrangement, are excluded. We reviewed this rule for v0.5 and kept it: the mediational literacy codes apply only to included documents.
• Review thresholds (R12). An episode is flagged for review when fewer than three of five dimensions are coded, when adjacency coherence falls below .67, or when the modal configuration is tied. Both thresholds remain provisional until we have coded data.
